; scenes.xon -- the kettle set: the links an errand is made of.
;
; (scene NAME GIVER . PROPS): the GIVER creature, one that talks, who
; (wants "thing") and, given it, (gives CLASS "name") or (gives goal).
; In the lines, {want} is the thing wanted and {where} the way to it
; from the giver's screen.  Each game draws a chain from these: a
; scene giving the goal stands in Kettle's square; what it wants,
; another scene gives, a screen farther out; the last want lies on the
; ground, or with its carrier (see items.xon).  The chain is read
; outward and paid inward.  Every way back from the goal runs five links
; deep, so the longest chain the valley holds, (chain 4 5), is always
; met (see choices.xon).

; Who has the ledger, and what they want for it.
(scene "the widow" "bailiff's widow" (wants "the pump-house key") (gives goal)
  (ask "My husband was the Guild's head bailiff.  Before he went below after"
       "the foreman's crew he put the Guild's ledger under the pump-house floor,"
       "and he did not come up.  It goes to the town, not the Guild.  The key"
       "went astray; there is one to be had {where}.")
  (again "The key, {where}.")
  (done "That is the key.  The ledger is the town's now; lay it on the well-head,"
        "and if they ask, Ada sent you."))
(scene "the clerk" "Guild clerk" (wants "a letter of the council") (gives goal)
  (ask "I copied the ledger before the Guild sealed it, and I will hand the"
       "copy over on the council's word and nothing less.  Bring me a letter"
       "of the council.  One was being drafted {where}.")
  (again "The council's letter, {where}.")
  (done "That is the council's hand.  Here is the copy, every page of it."))

; Who has the key.
(scene "the watchman" "night watchman" (wants "a flask of spirits") (gives token "the pump-house key")
  (ask "I have the pump-house key, and I have had a cold night every night"
       "since the pumps stopped.  A flask of spirits and the key is yours."
       "There is a flask to be had {where}.")
  (again "A flask, {where}, and the key is yours.")
  (done "Ah.  That warms.  The key; the lock sticks, so lift the door as you turn it."))
(scene "the smith" "smith" (wants "a sack of flour") (gives token "the pump-house key")
  (ask "I cut the pump-house lock and I can cut a key for it, but the forge is"
       "cold and so is the house.  The miller owes me a sack of flour, {where}."
       "Fetch it and I will cut your key.")
  (again "The flour first, {where}.")
  (done "There.  A key for the pump house, cut from memory; it will turn."))

; Who has a flask.
(scene "the ferryman" "ferryman" (wants "the ferry pole") (gives token "a flask of spirits")
  (ask "The flask is yours when the ferry runs, and it does not run without its"
       "pole, which the water took in the spring.  It fetched up {where}.")
  (again "The pole, {where}, and then the flask.")
  (done "That is the pole.  Here is the flask; leave some for the watchman."))
(scene "the innkeeper" "innkeeper" (wants "the lamp") (gives token "a flask of spirits")
  (ask "Spirits I have, but the cellar is dark since the lamp was taken off its"
       "hook.  A thief went out the back with it, {where}.")
  (again "My lamp, {where}.")
  (done "The lamp.  Here is a flask from the cellar, the last of the good cask."))

; Who has flour.
(scene "the miller" "miller" (wants "the mill pin") (gives token "a sack of flour")
  (ask "No flour grinds without the pin that holds the stone, and the pin fell"
       "in the race and washed down, {where}.")
  (again "The pin, {where}.")
  (done "The pin.  Give me an hour and the stone turns; take the sack by the door."))

; Who can get the council's letter.
(scene "the town surveyor" "town surveyor" (wants "the surveyor's chain") (gives token "a letter of the council")
  (ask "The Guild's surveyor went below with the foreman's crew and has not"
       "come up, so the council has me.  It will sign a letter when I show it"
       "the levels, and I cannot level without my chain.  A crow took the brass"
       "end of it, {where}.")
  (again "The chain, {where}.")
  (done "The chain.  The levels are what I said they were, and the council has"
        "signed.  Here is the letter."))
(scene "the councillor" "councillor" (wants "the sealed order") (gives token "a letter of the council")
  (ask "The council writes no letter against the Guild without the Guild's own"
       "sealed order in its hand.  The carter carried it out of town, {where}.")
  (again "The order, {where}.")
  (done "The Guild's own seal.  The council has written its letter; here."))
(scene "the carter" "carter" (wants "the lamp") (gives token "the sealed order")
  (ask "The order is in my cart under the sacks, and I do not unload in the"
       "dark.  My lamp was taken on the road, {where}.")
  (again "The lamp, {where}.")
  (done "A lamp.  The order, from under the sacks; it is sealed still."))

; Who has the ferry pole, the lamp, the mill pin, the brass of the
; chain: what was lost on the way out, found by someone farther out.
(scene "the eel-catcher" "eel-catcher" (wants "a coil of net twine") (gives token "the ferry pole")
  (ask "A pole came down the river into my weir, and I have been propping my"
       "nets on it.  Twine to mend them and I need no prop.  Twine is to be"
       "had {where}.")
  (again "Twine, {where}.")
  (done "That will mend them.  Take the pole; it was the ferry's, I suppose."))
(scene "the pedlar" "pedlar" (wants "a whetstone") (gives token "the lamp")
  (ask "I gave a road thief a penny for this lamp and asked him nothing.  It"
       "goes back for a fair trade: my whetstone cracked in the frost, and a"
       "pedlar with dull shears cuts no cloth.  There is a whetstone {where}.")
  (again "A whetstone, {where}.")
  (done "A good grit.  The lamp, then, and tell no one where you had it."))
(scene "the millwright" "millwright" (wants "a billet of seasoned oak") (gives token "the mill pin")
  (ask "That pin is in the bottom of the race and will stay there.  I can turn"
       "a new one, but not from green wood; it splits under the stone.  Find"
       "me a billet of seasoned oak, {where}.")
  (again "Seasoned oak, {where}.  Green will not do.")
  (done "Three summers dry at least.  Here is the pin, turned while you watched."))
(scene "the scrap-picker" "scrap-picker" (wants "a pair of hobnailed boots") (gives token "the surveyor's chain")
  (ask "The crows bring me what shines and I sell it on.  A brass chain, yes,"
       "I had it off a nest.  My boots are through at the toe, and the bog is"
       "cold.  Hobnailed boots, {where}, and the chain is yours.")
  (again "Boots, {where}.")
  (done "Dry feet.  The chain; every link is there, I counted them."))

; Who has the twine, the whetstone, the oak and the boots: the far
; valley, where the last want lies out on the ground.
(scene "the chandler" "chandler" (wants "a pot of pitch") (gives token "a coil of net twine")
  (ask "Twine I sell, and I would give a coil for the pitch I paid for and"
       "never had.  The cart that brought it turned over {where}.")
  (again "My pitch, {where}.")
  (done "Paid for twice, had once.  Here is the twine."))
(scene "the knife-grinder" "knife-grinder" (wants "a treadle strap") (gives token "a whetstone")
  (ask "My wheel turns on a leather strap, and the strap snapped and went"
       "into the ditch {where}.  No strap, no wheel; no wheel, no stone to spare.")
  (again "The strap, {where}.")
  (done "It turns.  Take the old stone; this one is new and finer."))
(scene "the woodcutter" "woodcutter" (wants "an iron wedge") (gives token "a billet of seasoned oak")
  (ask "I have oak stacked three summers, and I split none of it without my"
       "wedge.  I left it in a stump {where}, and the stump is still there.")
  (again "The wedge, {where}.")
  (done "That is the wedge.  A billet off the old stack; mind the grain."))
(scene "the cobbler" "cobbler" (wants "a roll of tanned hide") (gives token "a pair of hobnailed boots")
  (ask "Boots from what?  I have nails and no leather.  The tanner has a roll"
       "of hide to spare; the tanner is {where}.")
  (again "Hide, {where}.")
  (done "Good hide.  The boots; the nails are set close for the bog."))
(scene "the tanner" "tanner" (wants "a sack of oak bark") (gives token "a roll of tanned hide")
  (ask "No hide tans without bark, and my bark is cut and bagged and lying"
       "where I left it, {where}.  The smell keeps people off, mostly.")
  (again "The bark, {where}.")
  (done "Bark.  Take the roll from the top of the pile; it is the best of them."))
